## Why This Is Asked
Tests multi-cloud, multi-env orchestration, and robust gating. It probes backend scoping, provider aliasing, and policy-as-code integration in a realistic production-like flow.

## Key Concepts
- Per-env Terraform backends and state isolation
- Provider aliasing for multi-cloud deployments
- Policy-as-code gates (Sentinel/OPA) for prod safety
- Wrapper modules for consistent tagging across clouds

## Code Example
```javascript
// backend.tf (Terraform S3 backend per environment)
terraform {
  backend "s3" {
    bucket = "org-terraform"
    key    = "state/${var.environment}/terraform.tfstate"
    region = "us-east-1"
  }
}
```

```javascript
// Providers with aliases (multi-cloud)
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-east-1"
  alias  = "aws"
}
provider "google" {
  project = var.gcp_project
  region  = var.gcp_region
  alias   = "gcp"
}
```

```javascript
// Wrapper module usage for tags
module "shared_tags" {
  source      = "./modules/tags"
  environment = var.environment
  cost_center = var.cost_center
}
```

```javascript
// Simple OPA/rego style policy (example)
package terraform.policy
default allow = false
allow {
  input.environment != "prod"
}
```

```javascript
// CI gate steps (high level)
terraform init
terraform plan -out=tfplan
terraform show -json tfplan > plan.json
# Evaluate plan.json against policy (opa or sentinel)
```

## Why This Is Asked
- Tests for for_each on maps, dynamic blocks, and policy handling with Terraform. 
- Checks ability to compose minimal wrapper modules that feed into a shared VPC module without duplicating resources.
- Validates exporting a clean map of per-env ARNs for use by the VPC module.

## Key Concepts
- Terraform maps and for_each
- aws_iam_role and aws_iam_role_policy
- jsonencode for inline policies
- Module outputs and per-env composition

## Code Example
```hcl
variable "env_roles" {
  type = map(object({ enabled=bool, role_name=string, policy_json=string }))
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "env" {
  for_each = { for k,v in var.env_roles : k => v if v.enabled }
  name = each.value.role_name
  assume_role_policy = <<POLICY
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [{"Effect": "Allow", "Principal": {"Service": "ec2.amazonaws.com"}, "Action": "sts:AssumeRole"}]
}
POLICY
}

resource "aws_iam_role_policy" "env_inline" {
  for_each = aws_iam_role.env
  role     = each.key
  policy   = each.value.policy_json
}

output "role_arns" {
  value = { for k,v in aws_iam_role.env: k => v.arn }
}
```

